  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Eleven metres of the tether ribbon itself, laid up from drawn gall fibre in a flat braid nine centimetres wide and under two millimetres thick, cut from the spool when the works were cleared in 2297. The fibre is drawn from mature galls, retted, spun and laid up wet, and the whole of the material and the method is local. A sample tested to failure in 2299 took rather more than the design load, which is in the file and is not the part of the file anybody reads. The section is clean, uncorroded and still coiled on its original drum.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
